cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Novum Pipeline
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alberto
    family-names: Sola
    email: albertosola2002@gmail.com
    affiliation: Università degli Studi di Torino (UniTo)
repository-code: "https://github.com/GenRegDSCB/novum_pipeline"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Snakemake workflow for predicting miRNA targets in
  bacterial coding sequences with RNAhybrid and IntaRNA
  running as parallel arms. Optionally calibrates
  RNAhybrid's extreme-value statistics per miRNA via
  RNAcalibrate, so each query is scored against its own
  null distribution rather than a single species default;
  IntaRNA can be run with or without RNA accessibility
  correction in the same invocation. RNAhybrid is
  parallelised across (miRNA × target chunk) pairs with
  GNU Parallel, IntaRNA uses its native multithreading.
  Each arm's raw output is tidied, annotated with
  FASTA-derived gene/locus/protein metadata, and rendered
  as a human-readable alignment summary; the RNAhybrid
  arm is optionally plotted with ggplot2. A bundled
  PyWebView GUI provides a no-CLI interface for editing
  the config and launching runs.
keywords:
  - snakemake
  - pipeline
  - RNAhybrid
  - IntaRNA
  - miRNAs
  - genomes
  - bacteria
  - python
  - tidyverse

